                    AwakeningSection(heading: "The Free Energy Principle", body: "Karl Friston's Free Energy Principle (2010) might be the most important theory in neuroscience this century. It says:\n\nYour brain's primary job is to minimize prediction error.\n\nEvery moment, your brain generates a model of what SHOULD happen next — based on everything it's learned. Then it compares that prediction to what actually happens. The difference = prediction error.\n\nHigh prediction error = surprise = the brain mobilizes resources to deal with it.\nLow prediction error = everything is as expected = the brain can relax.\n\nThe brain minimizes prediction error in two ways:\n1. UPDATE THE MODEL (learning) — change your predictions to match reality\n2. CHANGE REALITY TO MATCH THE MODEL (action) — act on the world to make your predictions come true\n\nThis is called active inference. And it explains almost everything.\n\nANXIETY = chronically high prediction error. Your model keeps predicting threats that don't materialize, but instead of updating the model (\"maybe I'm safe\"), the brain doubles down on threat predictions.\n\nDEPRESSION = model that predicts nothing will work, so it stops generating actions. Low prediction error because it predicts nothing and gets nothing.\n\nSHADOW MATERIAL = high-precision priors (very confident predictions) that were written during trauma. They resist updating because the brain treats them as survival-critical. \"Never trust anyone\" was a reasonable prediction when written at age 8 after betrayal. At age 35, it's a miscalibrated prior generating chronic prediction error in every relationship."),
                    AwakeningSection(heading: "Meditation = Precision Recalibration", body: "Here's where it all connects.\n\nMeditation is NOT relaxation. It's not \"clearing your mind.\" It's precision recalibration of your predictive control system.\n\nStudy: Laukkonen & Slagter (2025) — Beautiful Loop Theory\nMeditation modulates the PRECISION of predictions at multiple levels of the processing hierarchy.\n\nFocused Attention meditation: Increases precision on selected signals (breath, body sensation) while decreasing precision on background noise (rumination, worry). You're training the brain to allocate prediction resources more efficiently.\n\nOpen Monitoring meditation: Reduces precision on ALL top-down predictions simultaneously. This allows the system to notice prediction errors it was previously ignoring — including shadow material that high-precision priors had been suppressing.\n\nThis is why meditation sometimes surfaces uncomfortable emotions. You're reducing the precision of the suppression model. The stuff you've been hiding from yourself becomes visible because the filter weakens.\n\nPSYCHEDELICS do the same thing, more dramatically. Psilocybin and DMT massively reduce the precision of top-down predictions (Carhart-Harris et al., REBUS model). The entire predictive hierarchy loosens. Everything that was suppressed surfaces at once. That's why psychedelic experiences can be profoundly therapeutic — and profoundly overwhelming.\n\nMeditation does it gradually. Psychedelics do it all at once. Same mechanism. Different dosage.\n\nStudy: Mount Sinai / IONS (2025)\n8 weeks of meditation practice shows deep-brain changes in memory and emotion regulation circuits — not just cortical surface changes. The recalibration reaches the subcortical systems where shadow material is stored.\n\nTHE DARK NIGHT REVISITED\nThe Dark Night of the Soul? In predictive coding terms: a catastrophic prediction error cascade. Your entire self-model — your identity, your beliefs, your life narrative — generates massive prediction errors because the old model is dissolving and the new one isn't online yet.\n\nYou're between firmware versions. The old OS is uninstalling. The new one is still downloading. Everything crashes.\n\nBut on the other side: a model with lower chronic prediction error. Less anxiety. Less projection. More accurate perception. Better calibrated priors.\n\nSt. John of the Cross called it passive purification. Friston would call it radical model update under high free energy. Same night."),
